PACKAGE CONTENTS:
 
Schematic based on the SVN trunk (latest) version

<top_level>
    |
    |-- config                    : Analysis configuration XML files
    |
    |-- data                      : Input data (templates from MC samples, etc)
    |      |----- lbne            : LBNE-specific inputs
    |      |----- lbno            : LBNO-specific inputs
    |
    |-- src                       
    |      |----- NDFit           : Near Detector Fit (Near Detector Flux and Cross-Section Systematics Constraint)
    |      |----- FDFit           : Far  Detector Fit (Oscillations)
    |
    |
    |-- macros                    : Our analysis procedures
    |     |------ spectra         : Macros used for testing nominal and tweaked spectra
    |     |         |-- nd
    |     |         |-- fd
    |     |
    |     |------ fit             : Macros used for fitting data or toy MC expts
    |     |         |-- nd
    |     |         |-- fd
    |     |
    |     |------ select          : Macros used for testing sample selections and constructing VALOR DSTs
    |
    |-- prod                      : Batch production scripts for RAL/IN2P3/Oxford farms
    |
    |-- root                      : The `valor_lbnx' (ROOT + VALOR framework+LBNx libraries) environment for our analysis macros
    |
    |-- setup                     : Environment setup scripts for various locations


............................................................................................................................

SETTING-UP YOUR ENVIRONMENT

Use the appropriate script from the setup directory.
The setup script expects two arguments: The top-level source code directory for the VALOR/LBNX and VALOR/FMWK packages.

Example:
% source setup/setup_at_XYZ.sh /path/to/lbnx/top/level/dir /path/to/fmwk/top/level/dir 

BUILDING THE VALOR CODE

% cd /path/to/lbnx/nuosc/top/level/dir
% ./configure --help
% ./configure <specify options or no options, autodetection of paths possible>
% make

RUNNING THE ANALYSIS CODE:

To run the VALOR/LBNX analysis ROOT macros, use `valor_lbnx' instead of `root'.
The valor_lbnx application is ROOT with all the VALOR/LBNX and VALOR/FMWK libraries loaded.
When running a VALO macro: 
% valor_lbnx 'macros/dir/some_script.C("/some/path/some/file.root",some_number)'
make sure there are NO spaces within ''.

